{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377568-increasing-soak-relearning-the-game","id":1377568,"title":"Increasing Soak- Relearning the Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-31T13:39:32-07:00","id":1377568,"title":"Increasing Soak- Relearning the Game","content":"A player wants to use Matter and Prime to strengthen his clothes to act as armor and allow him to soak Aggravated damage. Its seems doable with Matter 2/Prime 2, but I am unsure.<br /> <br /> Does this effect create additional health levels (like Skeletal Enhancement), create additional soak dice, or increase an attackers difficulty? Can any of these be picked?<br /> <br /> What if he uses a ritual to buy the necessary duration and effects to make it last the whole story? Is this a <i>trinket </i>and requires Prime 2, or does the extended duration mean he can carry it with him?<br /> <br /> Can he use a similar effect to sharpen his knife (Matter 2/Prime 2) to deal lower the difficulty or add extra damage levels? Both? Neither? Again, can he increase the duration and just take it with him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3097-gator-the-unread","name":"Gator the Unread","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T14:47:10-07:00","id":1377584,"title":"","content":"It would add increased soak dice. Enhanced health would be if one used Life, or Life + Prime to also soak aggravated damage.<br /> Increasing attack dificulty could be done with Forces (blurring the Mage, making them appear slightly off to where they are etc.) while making dodging easier would be using things like Correspondence 1 or Time 1.<br /> <br /> As for the question regarding the Trinket, yes, the enhanced clothes would be a trinket - and the effect could be made permanent.<br /> <br /> The sharpening of the knife would add extra damage dice, probably.<br /> <br /> The duration can be done as per the Damage &amp; Duration table - and as I said, could be made permanent, at least when it comes to the enhanced clothes. The knife, technically too - but it would probably still dull over time, just like the clothes would get shredded over time one way or the other..<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T14:48:48-07:00","id":1377585,"title":"","content":"Creates additional soak dice like armour. However if the get attacked by something that does agg they can only roll thouse dice to soak it.<br /> <br /> Permanency is kinda vague in the rules but I normally go ten successes on a ritual casting to make it so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T14:54:35-07:00","id":1377587,"title":"","content":"Making normal clothing act as armor just takes Matter 3. You can add Prime 2 too, but that would only protect your clothing-armor from direct attacks; armor generally applies to soaking Agg if armor would apply at all, so adding Prime just to have armor apply to Agg is unnecessary (though not pointless).<br /> <br /> The default option would be to increase soak dice, and would certainly classify the clothing as a trinket. Trinkets don't require Prime 2 if you can do the effect(s) you want without Prime. Trinkets are also generally permanent (Book of Secrets has a full crafting system if your ST doesn't want to use the normal duration chart rules and success just makes a permanent Trinket).<br /> <br /> Increasing health levels or increasing an attacker's difficult would be beyond just Matter to accomplish. If you want to increase health via armor, you'd need to add an effect that would redirect the damage from you to your clothing (thus risking destroying it) if you're not going to just use Life magic to do it. Increasing the difficulty to hit you would likewise be an effect beyond just making your clothing into armor as you'd need to add something that actually impedes the ability to hit you (Entropy or Correspondence are good choices here, though Forces can work too). You're also getting beyond Trinkets here, as these start to require the active effects found in more potent Wonders.<br /> <br /> A Trinket knife made with Matter 3 could probably get a -1 diff to attack/defend or +1 or +2 damage dice to represent how high quality it would be. Doing extra damage levels, applying Prime 2 to make it do Agg damage, and so on would elevate it beyond being a Trinket into more advanced Wonder making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T15:57:24-07:00","id":1377594,"title":"","content":"What I understand yawl said:<ul><li><i>My initial effect would add additional soak dice. </i></li> <li><i>Sharpening a knife should add to damage. </i></li> <li><i>Trinkets don't need prime if a mage can do the effect, so long as the mage pays for enough successes to meet the duration. </i></li> </ul>Okay, what if he is an cyborg and tries to use Matter to increase his soak dice by increasing ? Does he need Life as well to do that? At what level (I assume 2, maybe 3) does he need Life? Would it still require Matter 3?<br /> <br /> Provided the above works, or if the additional soak is applied to his armor, how much per success would the effect earn? One die per success? Two? Be based off the chart on page 504 of the Core book? <br /> <br /> Since the damage dealt my magic is in health levels and not damage dice, there is no soak...or is there? Is there an effect that provides an automatic success on soaking damage (that you can soak)? Since magic does automatic damage levels and heals automatic damage levels, shouldn't magic prevent automatic damage levels?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3097-gator-the-unread","name":"Gator the Unread","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T00:00:11-07:00","id":1377671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gator the Unread</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377568-increasing-soak-relearning-the-game?p=1377594#post1377594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trinkets don't need prime if a mage can do the effect, so long as the mage pays for enough successes to meet the duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or use the Wonder creation rules in Book of Secrets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, what if he is an cyborg and tries to use Matter to increase his soak dice by increasing ? Does he need Life as well to do that? At what level (I assume 2, maybe 3) does he need Life? Would it still require Matter 3? </div> </div> </div>What level of cyborg are we talking here?<br /> <br /> Though in general you'd need Life 3. Matter 3 if you need to impact your cybernetics as well (maybe Prime in this case depending on how magical the cybernetics are).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Provided the above works, or if the additional soak is applied to his armor, how much per success would the effect earn? One die per success? Two? Be based off the chart on page 504 of the Core book? </div> </div> </div>504. Though keep in mind you might not want to go that high in interests of keeping things from getting vulgar, and keeping things in the realms of Trinkets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since the damage dealt my magic is in health levels and not damage dice, there is no soak...or is there? </div> </div> </div>Unless otherwise stated, you get to soak regardless of an attack using damage dice or directly heath levels. If an attack rolls 4 damage, or deals 4 damage straight up, you're dealing with 4 damage in either case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there an effect that provides an automatic success on soaking damage (that you can soak)? Since magic does automatic damage levels and heals automatic damage levels, shouldn't magic prevent automatic damage levels? </div> </div> </div>There's nothing really stopping you from doing this, though it isn't generally going to be a passive effect on your armor, or a long running Life effect.<br /> <br /> The game also has a bias towards offense to avoid situations where it takes lots and lots of rounds to do anything between offense and defense are too evenly matched and nobody ever gets an advantage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T13:38:09-07:00","id":1377793,"title":"","content":"Thank you everyone for your replies. This has help immensely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3097-gator-the-unread","name":"Gator the Unread","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}